<title>FRANCE: Lyonnais rescue to be sent to EU late March - source.</title>
<headline>Lyonnais rescue to be sent to EU late March - source.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>A French state rescue package to prepare state-controlled bank Credit Lyonnais for privatisation will not be submitted for approval to the European Commission until late March, a Finance Ministry source said on Friday.</p>
<p>The rescue plan, the third in four years, had originally been expected to be lodged in Brussels by the end of this week.</p>
<p>&quot;Presentation of the plan has been delayed until the end of March,&quot; the source said. The source said the French ministry had agreed the delay with European Competition Commissioner Karel Van Miert to make various &quot;corrections and additions&quot; to the plan.</p>
</text>
